  'analyst.quality': { title: "The quality of what was created", body: "Four measures, each shown on its own rather than blended into one score: complete (every objective that counters a risk has a judgement of what it achieves, and the risk's impact is known), accepted by the CISO first time, in date (not past review), and consistent (no contradiction the record can find)." },
  'analyst.record': { title: "The record: the difference made", body: "What CIRKS records under the name in the last year: risks identified, judgements of what an objective achieves, risk scores lowered and the points that took off, actions built and completed, findings acted on, meetings attended. Printable, as evidence of the work." },
  'analyst.benefit': { title: "Where control changes bring the greatest benefit", body: "The top of the CISO's ranking: the control objectives not in place, ordered by the risk points putting each in place would remove, from the residuals judged on each risk. The full list, with costs, is on the CISO report." },
  'analyst.relationships': { title: "Where to build relationships", body: "Each department's risks at or above the action threshold with no security action planned and no exception, its unknown risk, the systems it relies on that others own, and its information asset owner and manager: the people to work with. A count of open work, never a measure of how active a colleague is." },
